.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Every other chaos-diagnostic tool in this gallery works on a DynamicalSystem with known equations of motion. Real experimental data doesn&#x27;t come with equations attached -- this example instead analyzes a single scalar time series, x(t), treating its true source -- here the Lorenz system, \dot{x}=\sigma(y-x), \dot{y}=x(\rho-z)-y, \dot{z}=xy-\beta z -- as unknown, and using only x(t) itself. It reconstructs an equivalent phase-space attractor by delay-coordinate (Takens) embedding,">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/chaos/chaos_metrics/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_timeseries_analysis_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/chaos/chaos_metrics/plot_timeseries_analysis`

